comments.message:
@paligill@gmail.com In the current implementations for ISL69269 and XDPE1X2XX, a reset command allows firmware changes to take effect immediately. In contrast, MPS VRs needed an AC cycle to let the new image take effect. As such, using ApplyTime=Immediate in the Redfish query was incorrect for MPS devices. The commit message has been updated to reflect the correct value: ApplyTime=OnReset.

However, the common VR update logic currently accepts both ApplyTime=Immediate and ApplyTime=OnReset [1]. If we want to enforce specific ApplyTime values based on the VR type, a separate patch should be introduced to implement that restriction explicitly.

[1] https://grok.openbmc.org/xref/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/i2c-vr/i2cvr_software_manager.cpp?r=466c66a3df6b295b851094480fd5513d790cfa67&mo=3060&fi=93#93
